+# Incidents brief: August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of 30 September.
+
+## 11 August: data ingest stall, full database disk
+
+- **Impact:** about 2.5 hours overnight with no new data; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Root cause:** one malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried endlessly; retry logs filled the database disk, briefly blocking writes.
+- **Fix:** restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then freed disk space (97% to 61%).
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+  - Paging escalation (Elif, Sunil): done; unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** public API unreachable for 47 minutes for nearly all clients.
+- **Root cause:** the certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently all month on an outdated credential.
+- **Fix:** renewed the certificate and restarted the API; renewal now uses the current credential and alerts on failure.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before certificate expiry (Priya): done.
+  - Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+  - Responders note their steps as they go (Mara): done, in on-call handover notes.
